inference_trace:
Sliding window over fruit indices: for a window [i, j] covering positions L=fruits[i][0], R=fruits[j][0], the minimum steps needed is `min(|startPos-L|, |startPos-R|) + (R-L)`. Expand `j`, shrink `i` while cost exceeds k, track max sum.

```java
class Solution {
    public int maxTotalFruits(int[][] fruits, int startPos, int k) {
        int n = fruits.length;
        int best = 0;
        long sum = 0;
        int i = 0;
        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++) {
            sum += fruits[j][1];
            while (i <= j && cost(fruits[i][0], fruits[j][0], startPos) > k) {
                sum -= fruits[i][1];
                i++;
            }
            if (i <= j) {
                best = (int) Math.max(best, sum);
            }
        }
        return best;
    }

    private long cost(int L, int R, int s) {
        long span = (long) R - L;
        long dl = Math.abs((long) s - L);
        long dr = Math.abs((long) s - R);
        return span + Math.min(dl, dr);
    }
}
```

