inference_trace:
Standard approach: bitmask DP over subsets. Sort, check total divisible by k, target = total/k. dp[mask] = true if the elements in mask can be arranged so that the current partial sum (sum(mask) % target) is being built, filling buckets greedily one at a time. Transition: from a reachable mask, add element i not in mask if sum(mask)%target + nums[i] <= target.

```java
class Solution {
    public boolean canPartitionKSubsets(int[] nums, int k) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int total = 0;
        for (int x : nums) total += x;
        if (total % k != 0) return false;
        int target = total / k;
        for (int x : nums) if (x > target) return false;
        boolean[] dp = new boolean[1 << n];
        int[] sum = new int[1 << n];
        dp[0] = true;
        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); mask++) {
            if (!dp[mask]) continue;
            int cur = sum[mask] % target;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                if ((mask & (1 << i)) != 0) continue;
                if (cur + nums[i] <= target) {
                    int next = mask | (1 << i);
                    if (!dp[next]) {
                        dp[next] = true;
                        sum[next] = sum[mask] + nums[i];
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[(1 << n) - 1];
    }
}
```

