inference_trace:
Classic bitmask DP: dp[mask] = min stickers to cover the set of target positions in mask. For each mask, apply each sticker greedily to uncovered positions.

```java
class Solution {
    public int minStickers(String[] stickers, String target) {
        int m = target.length();
        int n = stickers.length;
        int[][] cnt = new int[n][26];
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            for (char c : stickers[i].toCharArray()) {
                cnt[i][c - 'a']++;
            }
        }
        int full = (1 << m) - 1;
        int[] dp = new int[1 << m];
        java.util.Arrays.fill(dp, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
        dp[0] = 0;
        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << m); mask++) {
            if (dp[mask] == Integer.MAX_VALUE) continue;
            for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
                int[] avail = cnt[i].clone();
                int next = mask;
                for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                    if ((mask & (1 << j)) != 0) continue;
                    int c = target.charAt(j) - 'a';
                    if (avail[c] > 0) {
                        avail[c]--;
                        next |= (1 << j);
                    }
                }
                if (next != mask && dp[mask] + 1 < dp[next]) {
                    dp[next] = dp[mask] + 1;
                }
            }
        }
        return dp[full] == Integer.MAX_VALUE ? -1 : dp[full];
    }
}
```

