For each index i, the number of subarrays containing it is (i+1)*(n-i); odd-length ones are ceil of half of that.

```java
class Solution {
    public int sumOddLengthSubarrays(int[] arr) {
        int n = arr.length;
        int total = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int count = (i + 1) * (n - i);
            int odd = (count + 1) / 2;
            total += odd * arr[i];
        }
        return total;
    }
}
